## 🧩 Clean Architecture

The project follows Clean Architecture principles:

```text
banking-domain
      ↑
banking-application
      ↑
banking-api / banking-infrastructure
      ↑
banking-bootstrap
```

### Key Principles

* Domain logic does not depend on Spring.
* Application use cases do not depend on Spring.
* Infrastructure implements application output ports.
* API acts as an inbound adapter.
* Spring configuration is centralized in the bootstrap module.
* Dependencies point toward the core of the application.

---

## 📦 Modules

| Module                   | Responsibility                                            |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `banking-domain`         | Domain models, value objects, events, and business rules  |
| `banking-application`    | Use cases, commands, DTOs, and ports                      |
| `banking-infrastructure` | Kafka, Elasticsearch, repositories, and external adapters |
| `banking-api`            | REST controllers, validation, and API exception handling  |
| `banking-bootstrap`      | Spring Boot entry point and dependency wiring             |

---

## 🛠 Tech Stack

| Technology                | Usage                                    |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Java 21                   | Main programming language                |
| Spring Boot 3             | Application runtime and infrastructure   |
| Apache Kafka              | Asynchronous event streaming             |
| Spring Kafka              | Kafka producer, consumer, retry, and DLQ |
| Elasticsearch 8           | Transaction indexing and search          |
| Spring Data Elasticsearch | Elasticsearch repository integration     |
| Maven                     | Multi-module build system                |
| Docker                    | Containerization                         |
| Docker Compose            | Local infrastructure orchestration       |
| SpringDoc OpenAPI         | Swagger / API documentation              |
| JUnit 5                   | Unit testing                             |

